  <data key="d3">chunk-d6316acc831514d1f346d3599ee116c0</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763834865</data>
</node>
<node id="Table 2 — Translation BLEU scores and training FLOPs comparison (table)">
  <data key="d0">Table 2 — Translation BLEU scores and training FLOPs comparison (table)</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 2 compares BLEU on WMT14 EN-DE and EN-FR and estimated training FLOPs for various models. Transformer (big) achieves the highest single-model BLEU (EN-DE 28.4, EN-FR 41.8) while using far fewer FLOPs than large ensembles (e.g., 2.3×10^19 FLOPs vs ≈10^21 FLOPs for some ensembles), supporting claims of superior accuracy and efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-157bd100f04864e3700fd6674376be2d</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763834865</data>
</node>
<node id="Footnote 5: GPU TFLOPS estimates (K80, K40, M40, P100) (discarded)">
  <data key="d0">Footnote 5: GPU TFLOPS estimates (K80, K40, M40, P100) (discarded)</data>
  <data key="d1">discarded</data>
  <data key="d2">A footnote providing per-GPU sustained single-precision throughput estimates used to compute training FLOPs: K80=2.8 TFLOPS, K40=3.7 TFLOPS, M40=6.0 TFLOPS, P100=9.5 TFLOPS. It supports the paper's training-cost calculations and comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f63402f5fd9dc08a85abf13908faebed</data>
  <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1763834865</data>
</node>
